Subject: Reflective KV Llama Boundary
Description: P6 documented boundary for Ollama and llama-server reflective KV integration.

& [ReflectiveKVLlamaBoundary] is a documented blocked-boundary repository slice
  + [boundary_status] is blocked_pending_new_llama_cpp_or_llama_server_hook
  + [slice_scope] is documentation only
  + [runtime_integration_status] is not implemented
  + [policy_dependency] is P5 remains the authoritative default-off runtime policy gate
  + [safe_current_surface] is request, launch, cache_prompt, context-shift, runner lifecycle, and compatibility-patch observation
  + [unsafe_current_surface] is raw KV tensor mutation, direct attention-state mutation, or decode-time cache surgery through existing llama-server completion requests
  + [blocked_reason] is current cited Ollama and llama-server surfaces do not expose a safe raw KV or attention mutation hook

  + [go_kvcache_surface] is an in-process Go cache abstraction, not proof of llama-server runtime reachability
    @ [source] C:\Project\Ollama\kvcache\cache.go:15 defines the Cache interface
    @ [source] C:\Project\Ollama\kvcache\cache.go:19 exposes SetLayer
    @ [source] C:\Project\Ollama\kvcache\cache.go:25 exposes Get(ctx ml.Context)
    @ [source] C:\Project\Ollama\kvcache\cache.go:31 exposes Put(ctx ml.Context, key, value ml.Tensor)
    @ [source] C:\Project\Ollama\kvcache\cache.go:61 exposes StartForward(ctx, batch, reserve)
    @ [source] C:\Project\Ollama\kvcache\cache.go:64 exposes CopyPrefix
    @ [source] C:\Project\Ollama\kvcache\cache.go:69 exposes CanResume
    @ [source] C:\Project\Ollama\kvcache\cache.go:76 exposes Remove
    + [boundary_read] is useful for vocabulary and future test fixtures, but does not establish that live llama-server raw KV can be mutated from Go

  + [llm_server_interface_surface] is the Go request boundary over runner backends
    @ [source] C:\Project\Ollama\llm\server.go:59 defines LlamaServer
    @ [source] C:\Project\Ollama\llm\server.go:64 includes Completion
    @ [source] C:\Project\Ollama\llm\server.go:77 includes ContextLength
    @ [source] C:\Project\Ollama\llm\server.go:206 defines CompletionRequest
    @ [source] C:\Project\Ollama\llm\server.go:215 carries PreservedTokens and notes non-llama-server runners ignore it
    + [boundary_read] is safe for request gating and unsupported-runner no-op decisions, but it does not expose raw KV tensors or attention state

  + [llama_server_launch_surface] is the launch and HTTP completion boundary
    @ [source] C:\Project\Ollama\llm\llama_server.go:163 stores kvCacheType
    @ [source] C:\Project\Ollama\llm\llama_server.go:361 appends --cache-type-k and --cache-type-v
    @ [source] C:\Project\Ollama\llm\llama_server.go:651 appends --context-shift
    @ [source] C:\Project\Ollama\llm\llama_server.go:1114 defines llamaServerCompletionRequest
    @ [source] C:\Project\Ollama\llm\llama_server.go:1117 maps CachePrompt to json cache_prompt
    @ [source] C:\Project\Ollama\llm\llama_server.go:1280 sets CachePrompt from req.Shift
    @ [source] C:\Project\Ollama\llm\llama_server.go:1863 sends cache_prompt from req.Shift on an alternate request path
    @ [source] C:\Project\Ollama\llm\llama_server.go:2354 reads KV head count for memory estimation
    @ [source] C:\Project\Ollama\llm\llama_server.go:2362 estimates KV cache memory
    + [boundary_read] is appropriate for launch/request observation and cache_prompt/context-shift gating
    + [blocked_read] is cache_prompt requests prompt-cache reuse behavior, not arbitrary raw KV or attention mutation

  + [scheduler_surface] is runner lifecycle, reuse, context-shift, and load ownership
    @ [source] C:\Project\Ollama\server\sched.go:137 defines resolveContextShift
    @ [source] C:\Project\Ollama\server\sched.go:187 reuses a loaded runner when needsReload is false
    @ [source] C:\Project\Ollama\server\sched.go:561 sets config.ContextShift
    @ [source] C:\Project\Ollama\server\sched.go:562 constructs the LlamaServer
    @ [source] C:\Project\Ollama\server\sched.go:616 calls llama.Load
    @ [source] C:\Project\Ollama\server\sched.go:1337 evaluates needsReload
    + [boundary_read] is where a future trace-only or request-local P6 mode would need to avoid stale runner state
    + [blocked_read] is runner reuse and load control do not supply decode-time raw KV or attention mutation

  + [api_route_surface] is request-to-runner conversion and prompt preservation
    @ [source] C:\Project\Ollama\server\routes.go:205 defines scheduleRunner
    @ [source] C:\Project\Ollama\server\routes.go:624 starts a CompletionRequest in generate flow
    @ [source] C:\Project\Ollama\server\routes.go:633 passes PreservedTokens
    @ [source] C:\Project\Ollama\server\routes.go:2296 defines preservedTokensForCompletion
    @ [source] C:\Project\Ollama\server\routes.go:2323 clamps NumCtx to runner ContextLength
    @ [source] C:\Project\Ollama\server\routes.go:2756 sends a CompletionRequest in chat flow
    + [boundary_read] is useful for request/session citation, but route code should not own raw KV mutation

  + [llama_compat_surface] is the existing upstream patch isolation pattern
    @ [source] C:\Project\Ollama\llama\compat\README.md:1 names the llama.cpp compatibility layer
    @ [source] C:\Project\Ollama\llama\compat\README.md:16 states OLLAMA_LLAMA_CPP_SOURCE affects patch application
    @ [source] C:\Project\Ollama\llama\compat\README.md:36 lists loader hook points
    @ [source] C:\Project\Ollama\llama\compat\README.md:56 documents OLLAMA_LLAMA_CPP_COMPAT=0
    + [boundary_read] is the strongest current pattern for an isolated upstream patch, but the cited hook family is loader/model compatibility rather than runtime KV or attention mutation

  = must: keep P6 disabled unless P5 explicitly authorizes an active mode
  = must: treat request, launch, cache_prompt, context-shift, and scheduler controls as gates or trace surfaces only
  = must: require a new cited llama.cpp or llama-server hook before raw KV or attention mutation is attempted
  = must: keep any future llama.cpp change in a compat-style isolated patch with disable and rollback behavior
  = must: keep non-llama runners no-op or unsupported unless a later slice explicitly supports them
  = must: avoid launch-argument, request-field, runner-reload, memory-estimation, or compat-patch changes in this slice
  - never: approximate raw KV mutation through cache_prompt, context-shift, PreservedTokens, or Go-side route policy alone
  - never: claim runtime compatibility, memory behavior, latency behavior, or quality behavior without a buildable implementation and proof
